  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 935228c0fd2628c4db5028980babef0b, type: 3}
  m_Name: NarrativeParagraph
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.Tutorials.Editor::Unity.Tutorials.Editor.Paragraphs.NarrativeParagraph
  m_MaskingSettings:
    m_MaskingEnabled: 0
    m_UnmaskedViews: []
    MaskPreset: {fileID: 0}
  Text:
    m_Untranslated: 'You have successfully performed an object baking  to enable
      your project with truly natural grasps through VirtualGrasp.


      You have
      learned how to prepare the interactables, how to create the bake input file
      and how to use the BakingClient to communicate with the Cloud Baking Service
      to receive the bake output file.


      To finish this tutorial, you can now
      play your scene.'
--- !u!114 &4140261613178710283
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 1
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 935228c0fd2628c4db5028980babef0b, type: 3}
  m_Name: NarrativeParagraph
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.Tutorials.Editor::Unity.Tutorials.Editor.Paragraphs.NarrativeParagraph
  m_MaskingSettings:
    m_MaskingEnabled: 0
    m_UnmaskedViews: []
    MaskPreset: {fileID: 0}
  Text:
    m_Untranslated: VirtualGrasp only uses the geometrical mesh data of objects to
      generate grasps. To extract it, the model resources need to be marked as readable.
      <br/> The "Read/Write" flag on each model resource related to an interactable
      object needs to be checked.
